{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancelling a task has three primary effects:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It flags the task as canceled.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It causes any active cancellation handlers on the task to run, once.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It cancels any child tasks and task groups of the task, including","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"those created in the future. If those tasks have cancellation handlers,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they also are triggered.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Task cancellation is cooperative and idempotent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling a task does not automatically cause arbitrary functions on the task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to stop running or throw errors. A function "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"may"}]},{"type":"text","text":" choose to react"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to cancellation by ending its work early, and it is conventional to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"signal that to callers by throwing ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". However,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a function that doesn’t specifically check for cancellation will","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run to completion normally, even if the task it is running on is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"canceled. However, that function might still end early if it calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other code that handles cancellation by throwing and that function doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"handle the error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s safe to cancel a task from any task or thread. It’s safe for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiple tasks or threads to cancel the same task at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"time. Cancelling a task that has already been canceled has no","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"additional effect.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancel"},{"type":"text","text":" may need to acquire locks and synchronously run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arbitrary cancellation-handler code associated with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"canceled task. To reduce the risk of deadlock, it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recommended that callers release any locks they might be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"holding before they call cancel.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the task has already run past the last point where it could have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"performed a cancellation check, cancelling it may have no observable effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"Task.checkCancellation()","type":"codeVoice"}]}],"name":"See Also","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"See Also","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:isolation:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/task\/cancel()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CancellationError","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/isCancelled-swift.property","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/isCancelled-swift.type.property","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/checkCancellation()","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:isolation:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withTaskCancellationShield(operation:)-2lzl8","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withTaskCancellationShield(operation:)-8zlgh"],"title":"Canceling Tasks","anchor":"Canceling-Tasks","generated":true}],"metadata":{"conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Success","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Failure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"title":"cancel()","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"relatedModules":[],"name":"Swift"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","name":"iOS"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","name":"Mac Catalyst"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","name":"macOS"},{"unavailable":false,"be